#
# ## Configuration Comparison Guide
#
# ### To compare Base vs Extended Regressor:
#
# 1. **Run with `INCLUDE_CONTROL_IN_REGRESSOR = False`:**
#    - 6 weights: [Bias, Angle, Rate, Drag, Sin, Gyro]
#    - Compensates only for matched uncertainty Δ(x)
#    - Simpler, more stable
#
# 2. **Run with `INCLUDE_CONTROL_IN_REGRESSOR = True`:**
#    - 8 weights: [Bias, Angle, Rate, Drag, Sin, Gyro, **un**, **v**]
#    - Compensates for BOTH Δ(x) AND control effectiveness Λ
#    - Uses previous-step control to avoid algebraic loop
#    - Better for systems with Λ uncertainty
#
# ### When un/v weights matter:
# - If `Λ_true ≈ Λ_nom`: un/v weights stay near zero
# - If `Λ_true ≠ Λ_nom`: un/v weights become significant to compensate
#
# ### Test idea:
# Change `Lambda_true` to differ from nominal (e.g., `Lambda_true = 0.8 * np.diag([1/Jx, 1/Jy, 1/Jz])`) and observe how un/v weights adapt!

